# Commit messages

Format: `<type>[scope]: <imperative summary>` — lowercase after `:`, no period, ≤ 72 chars.

Types: `feat` `fix` `refactor` `chore` `docs` `test` `ci` `style` `perf` `build`

- Scope optional, lowercase: `feat(reqs): add user story guide`
- Body (optional): explain why, not the diff
- Footer: `Refs #123` / `Closes #123`; breaking → `type!:` + `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- MR title = commit subject; MR description = purpose, changes, tests, issues
- Avoid: vague (`update`, `WIP`), past tense (`added` → `add`), commit only when user asks

```text
feat(reqs): add user story guide
fix(auth): handle expired sessions
chore(release): v0.1.38
```
